cli-wireless-adopt = Make the ESP32 board on a front port the { -wireless(case: "lower") } module, replacing its firmware (a board the KVM left alone because it runs other firmware)
cli-wireless-adopt-port = The front port the board is on: keyboard, mouse or other
cli-wireless-adopt-firmware = The release folder to take the module's firmware from (default: the one that came with odkvmctl)
cli-adopting = The board on the { $port } port becomes the { -wireless(case: "lower") } module: waiting for it in its ROM…
cli-adopt-busy = this KVM has a { -wireless(case: "lower") } module already
cli-adopt-empty = nothing on the { $port } port
cli-adopt-not-taken = the board on the { $port } port didn't become the { -wireless(case: "lower") } module ({ $state })
